  "claim": "A famous wrestler used the move \"moonsault\" before it was made popular by others. His older brother performed in the World Championship Wrestling, after he left the World Wrestling Federation.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Randy Savage. Sentence: Randy Mario Poffo (November 15, 1952 – May 20, 2011), better known by the ring name \"Macho Man\" Randy Savage, was an American professional wrestler and color commentator best known for his time in the World Wrestling Federation (WWF, now WWE) and later World Championship Wrestling (WCW).\nPage: World Championship Wrestling. Sentence: World Championship Wrestling, Inc. (WCW) was an American professional wrestling promotion, historically based in Atlanta, Georgia.\nPage: Lanny Poffo. Sentence: He is also the real-life younger brother of \"Macho Man\" Randy Savage.\nPage: Moonsault. Sentence: Much of its popularity in both Japanese and American wrestling is attributed to The Great Muta, despite it being used in North America by \"Leaping\" Lanny Poffo years before Muta came from Japan.",
  "evidence_text": "Page: Randy Savage. Sentence: Randy Mario Poffo (November 15, 1952 – May 20, 2011), better known by the ring name \"Macho Man\" Randy Savage, was an American professional wrestler and color commentator best known for his time in the World Wrestling Federation (WWF, now WWE) and later World Championship Wrestling (WCW).\nPage: World Championship Wrestling. Sentence: World Championship Wrestling, Inc. (WCW) was an American professional wrestling promotion, historically based in Atlanta, Georgia.\nPage: Lanny Poffo. Sentence: He is also the real-life younger brother of \"Macho Man\" Randy Savage.\nPage: Moonsault. Sentence: Much of its popularity in both Japanese and American wrestling is attributed to The Great Muta, despite it being used in North America by \"Leaping\" Lanny Poffo years before Muta came from Japan.",
