        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "2a9e4ddf-db80-5a03-9d9b-c023b01169d0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Randy Savage, Lanny Poffo, The Great Muta\n- Organizations: World Wrestling Federation (WWF/WWE), World Championship Wrestling (WCW)\n- Places: Atlanta, Georgia, North America, Japan\n- Concepts: professional wrestling, color commentator, moonsault\n\nFacts:\n- Randy Savage, born Randy Mario Poffo on November 15, 1952, was an American professional wrestler and color commentator known by the ring name \"Macho Man\" Randy Savage.\n- Randy Savage was best known for his time in the World Wrestling Federation and later in World Championship Wrestling.\n- World Championship Wrestling, Inc. was an American professional wrestling promotion based in Atlanta, Georgia.\n- Lanny Poffo is the real-life younger brother of Randy Savage.\n- Lanny Poffo used the moonsault in North America years before The Great Muta came from Japan.\n- The Great Muta is credited with much of the moonsault's popularity in both Japanese and American wrestling.\n- Randy Savage died on May 20, 2011.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "ee49fc36-6d7a-5b52-92ea-2d0ffba2da86",
        "text": "Page: Randy Savage. Sentence: Randy Mario Poffo (November 15, 1952 – May 20, 2011), better known by the ring name \"Macho Man\" Randy Savage, was an American professional wrestler and color commentator best known for his time in the World Wrestling Federation (WWF, now WWE) and later World Championship Wrestling (WCW).\nPage: World Championship Wrestling. Sentence: World Championship Wrestling, Inc. (WCW) was an American professional wrestling promotion, historically based in Atlanta, Georgia.\nPage: Lanny Poffo. Sentence: He is also the real-life younger brother of \"Macho Man\" Randy Savage.\nPage: Moonsault. Sentence: Much of its popularity in both Japanese and American wrestling is attributed to The Great Muta, despite it being used in North America by \"Leaping\" Lanny Poffo years before Muta came from Japan.",
